From 99285c7f0cf14b07bf7c5c049fe76f4c895dc9e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zeng Xian <themezeng@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 10:29:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] chore: move pnpm settings to pnpm-workspace.yaml and declare
 dependency build policy (#1233)

* chore: move pnpm settings to pnpm-workspace.yaml and declare dependency build policy

pnpm 10 no longer reads the `pnpm` field in package.json, so `onlyBuiltDependencies`
and `overrides` there were inert and every pnpm command printed a warning. Move
`overrides` into `pnpm-workspace.yaml` and replace the stale build allowlist with an
explicit policy: `ignoreScripts: false`, `strictDepBuilds: true`,
`dangerouslyAllowAllBuilds: false`, and an `allowBuilds` map that decides every
script-bearing dependency. Only electron builds; the rest get their prebuilt binaries
through optionalDependencies or have no effect on this repo.

Keep npmmirror as the local registry for install speed and append registry.npmjs.org
in CI, so frozen-lockfile runs resolve from the canonical origin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CVRYPU4vS2MGKaUmnrBEks

* fix: align package builds with workspace policy

---------

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

